    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d852">

                <pb facs="0854" n="742" xml:id="pg742"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/5706: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wheeler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-19T11:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 19,
                                1919—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10:45
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>4240. The Russian Minister informs me that he is this morning in receipt of a
                    telegram from the Northwestern Army stating that Yudenitch has come to a satisfactory agreement with the
                    Esthonian Government and that all rumors that his troops are to be interned or
                    put under Esthonian command are false. American Mission’s 521[A].</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Wheeler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
